cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite the Governed Runtime Standards, please use the metadata in this file."
title: "Governed Runtime Standards: Action Provenance Record, Action Approval Attestation and Governed Runtime Profile"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
authors:
  - name: "Renly (XiPlatform Pty Ltd)"
    country: AU
    website: "https://renly.ai"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/XiPlatform/governed-runtime-standards"
url: "https://renly.ai/standards"
abstract: >-
  Open specifications for recording what AI agents do and on whose authority.
  The Action Provenance Record is a sealed, verifiable record of one action
  taken by or through an AI agent. The Action Approval Attestation binds a
  human approval to a digest of the exact proposed action, with a scope and
  bounds. The Governed Runtime Profile defines twelve testable guarantees for
  agent runtimes. Each specification has three conformance levels. Includes
  JSON Schemas, a zero-dependency TypeScript reference implementation and test
  vectors.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - provenance
  - accountability
  - audit
  - human-in-the-loop
  - approval
  - governance
  - specification
